Hi Michal,

I tried the requested UVC_QUIRK_FIX_BANDWIDTH workaround. For a direct
comparison, I used the same 320x240 YUYV mode at a requested 30 fps,
with exposure_dynamic_framerate=0.

The test was performed on:

7.1.8-200.xhci3d9eeb3.fc44.x86_64

This kernel contains both:

7c0c31c66a7f9daace156bac427aafb2f4bbb5fc
3d9eeb336131bc5a174367c384fa00c15c8744fd

IOMMU remained enabled in translated, strict mode, and there were no
DMAR or IOMMU faults.

I temporarily reloaded uvcvideo with quirks=0x80. The selected
streaming configuration changed from altsetting 7 with 3072 B/frame
to the following power-of-two configuration:

Device requested 1024 B/frame bandwidth
Selecting alternate setting 3 (1024 B/frame bandwidth)
Allocated 5 URB buffers of 32x1024 bytes each

Without dynamic debugging, one 300-buffer run completed with rc=0:

duration: 17.941 seconds
delivered buffers: 300
reported sequence gaps: 217
effective delivered rate: 16.72 fps
delivered positions: 58.03%

For comparison, the previous run in exactly the same video mode but
without quirks=0x80 selected altsetting 7 with 3072 B/frame and
produced:

duration: 31.065 seconds
delivered buffers: 300
reported sequence gaps: 620
effective delivered rate: 9.66 fps
delivered positions: 32.61%

Thus, quirks=0x80 reduced the reported gaps by about 65% and increased
the effective delivered rate by about 73%, although the stream was
still far from a smooth 30 fps.

I also ran five consecutive 120-buffer restarts without debugging.
All five completed with rc=0. In aggregate they delivered 600 buffers
in 38.736 seconds, with 441 reported sequence gaps:

effective delivered rate: 15.49 fps
delivered positions: 57.64%

The individual runs took between 7.120 and 8.422 seconds, corresponding
to effective delivered rates of approximately 14.25 to 16.85 fps.

A five-second xHCI tracepoint capture contained 39,136 queued isochronous
TRBs. All of them had this layout:

length=1024 td_size=0 tbc=0 tlbpc=0

There were no 3072-byte isochronous TRBs. The same trace interval
contained 339 Missed Service Error events.

In a separate five-second xHCI dynamic-debug interval I observed:

147 Miss service interval
0 Spurious event dma
0 All TDs skipped
0 Event dma ... not part of TD
0 Event TRB ... with no TDs queued
0 DMAR/IOMMU faults

The tracepoint and dynamic-debug counts came from separate intervals,
so the two Missed Service Error counts should not be compared directly.

This seems to show that avoiding the 3072-byte layout has a substantial
positive effect and removes the "Spurious event dma" messages in this
sample. However, it does not solve the problem: many service intervals
are still missed, and only about 15-17 frames per second are actually
delivered.

I have attached the complete results, including the raw 25 MB xHCI
trace, dynamic-debug log, UVC negotiation log, and stream logs:

fix-bandwidth-320x240-20260823-225712.tar.gz

SHA-256:

2e4016bdc4753d404a9e6b6f839ebbb8ce8a95957133430ed639914d4c66cf34

Regards,
Dmitry


